&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Tubi is looking for a culturally fluent, highly creative Social Media Manager to help identify and bring to life the unexpected opportunities that keep Tubi at the center of culture and close to our fans.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role will focus on cultural opportunity scouting, fandom and community marketing, and social-led activations. You&#39;ll be deeply tapped into what audiences are talking about, watching, sharing, and obsessing over, as well as, identifying the creators, communities, behaviors, and emerging moments where Tubi has a credible reason to participate.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Spotting the opportunity is only half the job. We&#39;re looking for someone who can turn cultural signals into ideas and then make them happen, whether that&#39;s an unexpected creator partnership, a community activation, a quick-turn stunt, an IRL fan moment, or something we haven&#39;t tried before.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll work closely with the broader Social team and partners across Brand, Content, PR, Creator, and other functions to help Tubi show up in ways that feel fan-first, culturally relevant, and unmistakably Tubi.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;This is a hybrid role based out of our Los Angeles office. You must be willing to travel to our Los Angeles&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;office two days/week.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You&#39;ll Do:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Scout emerging creators, communities, fandom behaviors, conversations, and cultural moments, turning the strongest signals into opportunistic partnerships and activations that expand where and how Tubi shows up in culture&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop social-first ideas and activations rooted in audience behavior and cultural momentum, from scrappy quick-turn opportunities to larger community stunts and partnerships&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead community-driven programs and activations across Tubi&#39;s priority fandoms, helping build sustained affinity beyond individual title launches&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own opportunities from idea through execution, including developing the strategic approach, building the business case, coordinating partners, managing timelines, and bringing the final experience to life&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate across Brand, Content, PR, CRM, B2B, Creative Studio, and other teams to identify ways successful social ideas can extend into broader marketing opportunities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bring a clear point of view on where Tubi should or shouldn&#39;t participate, balancing cultural relevance with brand fit and potential impact&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Evaluate activations and experiments to identify actionable learnings, shape future opportunities, and recommend where the team should iterate, invest, or take bigger swings&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your Background:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of experience in social media, cultural marketing, experiential, creator marketing, community, or a related field, ideally within entertainment or a culture-first consumer brand&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deeply fluent in internet culture, fandoms, creators, and online communities, with strong instincts for what&#39;s gaining momentum before it becomes obvious&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A creative thinker who naturally sees possibilities in audience behavior: you don&#39;t just notice what&#39;s happening, you immediately start thinking about what a brand could do with it&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Equally comfortable ideating and executing; you can take an interesting cultural observation and turn it into an actionable plan&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of what makes a brand&#39;s participation in culture feel credible versus forced&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Skilled cross-functional collaborator who can build enthusiasm around an idea while navigating stakeholders, approvals, and operational realities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent communicator with the ability to clearly articulate the cultural insight, creative idea, and business rationale behind a recommendation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Passionate about entertainment and deeply curious about the communities that form around TV, movies, creators, and culture, with strong creative taste and a high bar for execution&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
