&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Tubi is creating a Performance Partner role to focus on supporting managers end-to-end in developing and managing their teams. This role will own the end-to-end Performance Improvement Plan (PIP) process, partner closely with HRBPs to develop and execute strategic talent programs, and drive manager effectiveness across the organization. This is a highly visible role that sits at the intersection of performance management, talent strategy, and manager enablement — ideal for someone who wants to build and own a program from the ground up.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is an individual contributor role reporting to our VP of People. This role will be hybrid and can be based in SF/NYC/LA/Toronto.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You&#39;ll Do:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the end-to-end Performance Improvement Plan (PIP) process — from initial documentation through execution, check-ins, and resolution — partnering with legal, managers and business leaders throughout&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with HRBPs on HR programs for their teams (e.g., performance reviews, onboarding, promotions), bringing performance management expertise into broader talent initiatives&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and execute strategic talent programs that drive manager effectiveness, bringing workforce trends and analytics into program design&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advise managers on trade-offs when navigating complex, undefined performance issues; encourage experimentation and iteration in how managers approach team development&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead multi-team efforts related to performance and manager effectiveness (e.g., a performance refresh, a new PIP framework rollout), building trust and credibility across functions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Balance competing demands across multiple concurrent PIPs and programs, orchestrating initiatives to deliver business-ready outcomes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coach managers directly on how to have difficult performance conversations, set clear expectations, and document performance issues appropriately&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track and analyze trends across PIPs and performance interventions, sharing insights with HRBPs and People leadership to inform broader talent strategy&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;More About You&lt;/strong&gt;:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You can hold structure and empathy at the same time — able to guide a manager through a difficult PIP while keeping the process fair, consistent, and legally sound&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You&#39;re comfortable owning a program end-to-end, including solving complex and undefined problems as they arise&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You build trust quickly across HRBPs, managers, and cross-functional partners, and can lead multi-team efforts without formal authority&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You bring workforce trends and data into your recommendations, rather than relying on instinct alone&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You can balance multiple active PIPs and programs simultaneously without losing quality or consistency&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You&#39;re not afraid to have hard conversations, and you can coach others (especially managers) through having them too&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You&#39;re detail-oriented and process-minded, but flexible enough to adapt your approach as each situation demands&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your Background:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3+ years of HR, People Operations, or HRBP experience within a high-growth company, with direct experience managing performance improvement processes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience partnering with HRBPs or business leaders to design and execute HR programs for a team or function&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to solve complex, undefined HR problems and advise on trade-offs in ambiguous situations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience coaching managers on performance management, difficult conversations, and documentation best practices&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong track record of using HR data and workforce trends to inform program design and decision-making&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leading or contributing to multi-team initiatives (e.g., systems rollouts, performance process refreshes)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge and experience with HR tools, performance management systems, and data/reporting techniques&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Workday experience; other HRIS systems a plus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;BA/BS degree from a four-year accredited university preferred&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong writing skills, particularly for performance documentation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
