&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Tubi is seeking a strategic and agile Sr. HRBP (Tech) to help us build a world-class People team responsible for providing high-quality support to employees, in close partnership with functions such as Talent Management, Total Rewards, Talent Acquisition, and Workplace. The Sr. HRBP (Tech) will act as a strategic thought partner to leaders across our Engineering and Product organizations, and tackle org issues with people-focused solutions aligned with business goals. This role will be responsible for empowering a culture of high performance, retaining and engaging talent, and driving velocity through simplicity across the tech team.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role is critical to scaling a high-growth organization and driving operational efficiency across the People Team. You&#39;ll have a direct impact on the employee experience at Tubi — come bring your bright ideas to the team!&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is an individual contributor role reporting to our VP of People. This role will be hybrid, based in SF.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You&#39;ll Do:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with tech management to support initiatives by understanding organizational objectives, issues, needs, and key success factors&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide strategic business partnership and coaching to all levels of leadership&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and drive talent programs to shape and reinforce our cultural values and mission&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage our annual talent cycle, inclusive of compensation planning and execution&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proactively assess team and employee development needs, anticipate risks and unintended consequences, and lead iteration cycles on ambiguous or undefined problems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own stakeholder alignment across Talent Management, Talent Acquisition, and other cross-functional partners, facilitating collaboration at scale to drive efficiencies and simplify workflows&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead a talent vertical or key initiative (e.g., leadership development, employee engagement/enablement, career pathing) in partnership with the People Programs team, measuring impact and iterating over time&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage the administrative responsibilities of the People Operations team, performing operational duties required to keep our processes running efficiently and effectively&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support our onboarding program to ensure seamless integration of new hires into Tubi&#39;s culture and community&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conduct off-boarding, analyze trends, and share opportunities with executives to influence/inform decisions, modeling urgency and a bias toward iteration in high-impact programs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage compliance programs, including annual reporting, mandatory filings, policy updates, and employee training&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;More About You&lt;/strong&gt;:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You can successfully strike the right balance of being an advisor to the business but also an advocate for employees&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You will be a whiz with project management, change management, and driving programs independently, even when the path forward is ambiguous or undefined&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are hyper-focused on delivering results in a fast-paced environment, with the judgment to anticipate risk before it surfaces&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You can think big and execute the smallest of details equally well&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of the Technology and Media space, understanding trends, and bringing great ideas to the table&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understand people dynamics, organizational strategy, and talent processes, and can align HR strategies to org-level KPIs as business needs shift&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You&#39;re able to negotiate sensitive situations with confidence and finesse&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You can hit the ground running with little guidance/direction&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are not afraid to speak out, own stakeholder alignment, and shape high-visibility programs/initiatives&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborative team player who facilitates collaboration across functions at an org-wide scale and isn&#39;t afraid to roll up your sleeves&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your Background:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of HR or People Operations experience within a high-growth company&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3+ years supporting technical functions like Engineering and Product&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3+ years of designing and implementing talent management and employee experience programs, ideally owning a vertical (e.g., L&amp;amp;D, DEIB, people systems) rather than a single initiative&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience supporting tech organizations and coaching executives&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience creating, owning, and driving strategic company-wide initiatives and programs, and measuring their impact to iterate over time&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Passionate about company culture and experienced in shaping the right values&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong analytical skills and logical thought processes with the ability to identify, resolve, and anticipate risk in sophisticated and sensitive HR issues/problems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong track record of using HR data to drive solutions and influence leaders as business context shifts&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven effective partner management and collaboration with other teams, including owning stakeholder alignment for major cross-functional programs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge and experience with HR tools, applicant tracking systems, and data management/reporting techniques&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience creating and fostering partnerships with internal leadership and executive teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Workday experience; other HRIS systems a plus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;BA/BS degree from a four-year accredited university preferred&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong business acumen and writing skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
