&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are hiring a Senior Software Engineer to build Tubi&#39;s native app runtime for connected TVs on Cobalt, the lightweight, open-source browser engine behind YouTube on living room devices. You will own the layer between Tubi&#39;s React app and the device: the Cobalt engine, its Starboard porting layer, and new native components we write in C++ and Rust.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The goal is a Tubi app that launches faster, uses less memory, and behaves the same on every device, starting with Fire TV and expanding to other CTV platforms. This is a hands-on, high-ownership role on a small team, working closely with our web engineers, QA, and device partners.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a hybrid role which is two days in the SF office.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You&#39;ll Do:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build, integrate, and ship Cobalt as the runtime for Tubi&#39;s CTV apps, packaged as a native library inside our Android (Fire TV) app and later on other platforms&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Implement and maintain Starboard platform integrations: graphics, input, audio/video playback, DRM, and system services&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Write new native modules in modern C++ and Rust, including safe FFI boundaries between the two&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive startup and memory performance on low-end, memory-constrained devices (1 GB RAM class): profile, measure, and fix&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Keep us current with upstream Cobalt releases, track and contribute fixes upstream, and manage security patches for the engine we ship&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with media and playback teams on video pipeline needs such as demuxing, adaptive streaming, and ad playback&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build tooling that runs the Tubi app on Cobalt on developer machines and in CI, so we can test UI and automation without a device farm&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work directly with device partners&#39; engineering teams on platform issues&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mentor engineers and raise the team&#39;s native and systems engineering bar&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your Background:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;6+ years of professional software engineering, most of it in systems or native code&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Expert-level modern C++ (C++17/20): memory management, concurrency, templates, and debugging large codebases&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong production experience in Rust: ownership and lifetimes, async, unsafe code, and C/C++ interop (FFI, bindgen/cxx)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with large C++ build systems (GN/Ninja, CMake, or Bazel) and cross-compiling for ARM and embedded Linux or Android targets&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on performance work: profiling CPU, memory, and startup time with tools like perf, Perfetto, or heaptrack, and turning findings into measurable wins&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort debugging on real hardware: Android NDK, adb, native crash analysis, and symbolication&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Clear written communication and a track record of leading technical initiatives across teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Nice to Have&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with Cobalt, Starboard, Chromium, or another browser engine (Blink, WebKit, Servo)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;JavaScript engine internals, especially V8: code caching, snapshots, or GC tuning&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Graphics on embedded devices: OpenGL ES, Skia, or WebGPU&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Media pipelines: MSE/EME, ExoPlayer or native players, demuxers, Widevine or PlayReady DRM&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Shipping on TV platforms such as Fire TV, Android TV, Samsung Tizen, LG webOS, or Roku&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Open-source contributions to C++ or Rust projects&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Enough React and TypeScript to work with the web app running on top of the engine&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
